 \nL135:   * Maintain BUY and cut target price from Rmb585.00 to Rmb470.00.\nL136: 【33†Image: 01-3q26-results.png】\nL137: ## Analysis\nL138:   * 3Q26 results came in below estimates with GAAP net profit of Rmb21,246m (+14.5% yoy/-5.8% qoq) and adjusted net profit of Rmb18,862m (+14.9% yoy/-9.8% qoq), vs our estimate of Rmb23.92b. This brings 9M26 net profit and adjusted net profit to Rmb64,530m (+31.6% yoy) and Rmb57,876m (+32.7% yoy) respectively, representing 69% of our full-year estimates of Rmb93,637m (+29.7% yoy) and Rmb83,659m (+29.7% yoy). The earnings miss stemmed from margin contraction.\nL139:     * Battery shipment grew 44.4% yoy and 12.1% qoq to Rmb260 GWh in 3Q26, in line with estimates, including 195 GWh EV battery (+35.4% yoy/+12.1% qoq) and 65 GWh energy storage system (ESS) battery (+80.6% yoy/+12.1% qoq).\nL140: 【34†Image: 02-key-financials.png】\nL141: \nL142: Company Coverage\nL143: ## Contemporary Amperex Technology Co (300750 CH): 3Q26: Earnings Miss Due To Delayed Pass-through Of Tax Hikes\nL144: \nL145: Thursday, 22 October 2026\nL146: \nL147: Hong Kong / China\nL148: \nL149: Share\nL150: \nL151: Listen\nL152: \nL153: Search\nL154: \nL155:   * 【28†Equities】\nL156:   * 【29†China】\nL157: ## Highlights\nL158:   * 3Q26 net profit missed expectations at Rmb21.25b (+14.5% yoy/-5.8% qoq), as CATL bore the export VAT hikes and 2% consumption tax, and had not passed on to customers yet.\nL159: \nL160:   * We expect margins to recover in 3Q26, as the tax rate hikes will be partly passed through to customers via higher battery prices. Having said that, the further roll-back of tax concession in 2027 will remain a drag on margins.\nL161:   * We cut our 2026-28 net profit forecasts by 5%/10%/16% to Rmb89,121m/Rmb104,895m/Rmb116,370m respectively, as we now expect CATL to bear part of the tax hikes.\nL162: \nL163:   * Maintain BUY and cut target price from Rmb585.00 to Rmb470.00.\nL164: 【33†Image: 01-3q26-results.png】\nL165: ## Analysis\nL166:   * 3Q26 resu